    "issue_alignment": "The issue states parse_to_param() does not check for the end of data when encountering an escape character or the start of a value. The escape branch (case '\\\\', status PARA_VALUE_QUOTED) dereferences *(tmp+1) unconditionally; when the parameter's quoted value ends with a backslash that is the final byte of the message (tmp == end-1), the read of *(tmp+1) goes one byte past the input buffer (heap-buffer-overflow). The value-start branch sets param->value.s = tmp+1 without an end check, allowing value.s to point past the data."
